WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.944
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.244 --> 00:00:08.723
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.023 --> 00:00:14.973
Unit fifteen: Pop Culture. Today you will describe recent trends with the present perfect.

4
00:00:15.273 --> 00:00:17.693
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.633 --> 00:00:22.040
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.883 --> 00:00:24.001
Trending topic.

7
00:00:25.017 --> 00:00:28.491
Trending topic means a subject many people discuss online now.

8
00:00:29.083 --> 00:00:31.257
The concert is a trending topic.

9
00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:34.700
Your turn. Say: Trending topic.

10
00:00:37.533 --> 00:00:38.627
Trending topic.

11
00:00:39.383 --> 00:00:40.257
Meme.

12
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:44.538
Meme means a funny picture or video shared online.

13
00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:46.871
That meme made everyone laugh.

14
00:00:47.483 --> 00:00:49.741
Your turn. Say: Meme.

15
00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:53.508
Meme.

16
00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:55.785
Celebrity culture.

17
00:00:56.783 --> 00:01:00.873
Celebrity culture means society's great interest in famous people.

18
00:01:01.483 --> 00:01:03.878
Celebrity culture affects young people.

19
00:01:04.483 --> 00:01:07.403
Your turn. Say: Celebrity culture.

20
00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:11.767
Celebrity culture.

21
00:01:12.517 --> 00:01:13.286
Fandom.

22
00:01:14.283 --> 00:01:17.165
Fandom means all the fans of something, as a group.

23
00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:19.796
The K-pop fandom is huge.

24
00:01:20.383 --> 00:01:23.152
Your turn. Say: Fandom.

25
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:26.850
Fandom.

26
00:01:27.617 --> 00:01:28.908
Viral challenge.

27
00:01:29.917 --> 00:01:33.426
Viral challenge means an online activity that spreads quickly.

28
00:01:34.017 --> 00:01:36.190
The dance became a viral challenge.

29
00:01:36.783 --> 00:01:39.865
Your turn. Say: Viral challenge.

30
00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.165
Viral challenge.

31
00:01:44.917 --> 00:01:46.011
Pop icon.

32
00:01:47.017 --> 00:01:49.864
Pop icon means a very famous pop star.

33
00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:52.450
She is a pop icon in Asia.

34
00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:56.097
Your turn. Say: Pop icon.

35
00:01:58.933 --> 00:01:59.911
Pop icon.

36
00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:01.837
Mainstream.

37
00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.976
Mainstream means liked or accepted by most people.

38
00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:08.467
This music is now mainstream.

39
00:02:09.083 --> 00:02:11.817
Your turn. Say: Mainstream.

40
00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:15.691
Mainstream.

41
00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:17.637
Subculture.

42
00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:22.020
Subculture means a smaller group with its own style.

43
00:02:22.617 --> 00:02:24.593
Skateboarding is a subculture.

44
00:02:25.183 --> 00:02:27.859
Your turn. Say: Subculture.

45
00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:31.933
Subculture.

46
00:02:32.683 --> 00:02:33.951
Influence.

47
00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:38.180
Influence means the power to change how people think.

48
00:02:38.783 --> 00:02:41.154
Social media has a big influence.

49
00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.298
Your turn. Say: Influence.

50
00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.065
Influence.

51
00:02:48.817 --> 00:02:49.818
Phenomenon.

52
00:02:50.817 --> 00:02:54.082
Phenomenon means something unusual that many people notice.

53
00:02:54.683 --> 00:02:56.590
The game was a global phenomenon.

54
00:02:57.183 --> 00:02:59.720
Your turn. Say: Phenomenon.

55
00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:03.498
Phenomenon.

56
00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:04.880
Buzz.

57
00:03:05.883 --> 00:03:08.370
Buzz means excitement and talk about something.

58
00:03:08.983 --> 00:03:10.844
There's a lot of buzz about the film.

59
00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:13.696
Your turn. Say: Buzz.

60
00:03:16.533 --> 00:03:17.314
Buzz.

61
00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:19.411
Cultural impact.

62
00:03:20.417 --> 00:03:23.751
Cultural impact means the effect something has on society.

63
00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:26.640
Her songs had a big cultural impact.

64
00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:30.251
Your turn. Say: Cultural impact.

65
00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.484
Cultural impact.

66
00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:39.218
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:40.083 --> 00:03:42.710
Visal, have you seen the new dance challenge?

68
00:03:43.817 --> 00:03:47.700
Yes! It has become a viral challenge in just one week.

69
00:03:48.783 --> 00:03:50.736
Why is it so popular?

70
00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:57.019
A pop icon started it, and her fandom shared it everywhere.

71
00:03:58.117 --> 00:03:59.745
Has it influenced your friends?

72
00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:06.210
Definitely! It has influenced many teenagers. Even my teacher tried it!

73
00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:09.076
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:09.917 --> 00:04:13.298
Grammar focus: Present perfect for recent events.

75
00:04:13.598 --> 00:04:14.831
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:15.517 --> 00:04:17.296
The trend has become popular.

77
00:04:18.183 --> 00:04:20.229
It has influenced many teenagers.

78
00:04:21.117 --> 00:04:23.221
The video has just gone viral.

79
00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:27.513
Use the present perfect for recent events with a result now.

80
00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:32.412
Be careful! Don't say: The trend has became popular.

81
00:04:34.367 --> 00:04:37.005
Say: The trend has become popular.

82
00:04:37.305 --> 00:04:39.095
Become, became, become.

83
00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.854
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:43.667 --> 00:04:44.761
Going Viral.

85
00:04:45.061 --> 00:04:47.931
The viral challenge became a trending topic overnight.

86
00:04:48.933 --> 00:04:51.746
It has become a real phenomenon with lots of buzz.

87
00:04:52.733 --> 00:04:57.020
Celebrity culture and fandoms often shape mainstream pop culture.

88
00:04:58.033 --> 00:05:02.250
Some trends start in a small subculture, then become popular.

89
00:05:03.267 --> 00:05:06.822
Memes and challenges have had a big cultural impact and influence.

90
00:05:07.933 --> 00:05:11.714
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:14.422
The trend has blank popular.

92
00:05:14.722 --> 00:05:18.549
A, become. B, became. C, becomes.

93
00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:23.867
The answer is A: become.

94
00:05:25.017 --> 00:05:28.003
All the fans of something, as a group, is a blank.

95
00:05:28.303 --> 00:05:32.212
A, fandom. B, meme. C, subculture.

96
00:05:35.767 --> 00:05:37.615
The answer is A: fandom.

97
00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:41.353
Excitement and talk about something is blank.

98
00:05:41.653 --> 00:05:45.318
A, buzz. B, influence. C, a phenomenon.

99
00:05:48.867 --> 00:05:50.704
The answer is A: buzz.

100
00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:55.249
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:56.083 --> 00:05:59.604
What trend in pop culture do you find interesting?

102
00:06:08.417 --> 00:06:09.882
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:10.182 --> 00:06:19.417
I find K-pop interesting. It has become popular all over the world, and it has influenced fashion and dance in Cambodia.

104
00:06:19.717 --> 00:06:21.450
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:27.185
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and present perfect for recent events.

106
00:06:27.485 --> 00:06:32.250
Today's value is critical thinking. Think carefully and give reasons for your opinions.

107
00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:35.214
See you in Unit sixteen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:35.514 --> 00:06:39.026
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

